  The reel_script states that the Kerala irrigation department has been accused of releasing water through the sluice gates after 40 ft during heavy rain, but the article describes this as their routine practice and does not mention an accusation; it is presented as a plain fact (the article says it was the routine during the DMK rule). The reel_script also wrongly frames it as the DMK government era's accusation.
  The reel_script says the Coimbatore Corporation officials are 'maintaining good relations' with Kerala officials, which is a fair reading, but the reel_script says the corporation officials 'have already talked and prepared an estimate' while the article says they prepared the estimate with the Kerala irrigation department, which the draft roughly matches; however the slides_spec 'அணை பராமரிப்பு' slide text is cut off mid-sentence ('சரி செய்ய மாநகராட்சி அதிகாரிகள் கேரள') and is ungrammatical and unclear.
  The reel_script and caption say the 40 ft rise and 'this first week' rain situation, but the article says the rain did not fall in the city area; the reel_script states 'இந்த முதல் வாரத்தில் நகர் பகுதியில் மழை இல்லை' which is consistent, but it omits the article's point that the city's rain was expected but absent, which is minor.
